a4cceafe6b01909b2277c8e6f9cc53d0"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G7","usage":{"input_tokens":234618,"output_tokens":2246,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"d2f5f7a60732097bb0cf000eb40d9655a81fda2d448728845854555a0cff1d3e"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":67892,"output_tokens":3727,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the two conflicting definitions of docker_unaccounted_bytes (Design says 'overlay2 truth − ledger'; AC says 'du root truth − docker system df') to a single same-domain subtraction, and state which du reading is the minuend.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4357,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design: 'docker_unaccounted_bytes is overlay2 truth − ledger, clamped at 0.'","AC: 'docker_unaccounted_bytes (= du truth minus docker system df)'","The ledger sums images + containers + build cache, which reside across the whole /var/lib/docker root, not only overlay2 — so the two operands must share the same measurement domain (whole-root du vs whole-root ledger) for the delta to be meaningful."],"finding":"The plan defines docker_unaccounted_bytes two incompatible ways: the Design section says 'overlay2 truth − ledger' while the AC says 'du truth minus docker system df' (whole root). Since the ledger (images+containers+build cache) spans the whole Docker root, subtracting it from an overlay2-only measurement is a mismatched-domain subtraction that skews the residue and defeats the metric's purpose.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f717a4e5162de2e86","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design §'Detecting the bytes docker system df cannot see' vs AC line for observability.sh (docker_unaccounted_bytes)","norm_id":"n14dd1e91aaf247e4","priority":0.3643,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer follows the Design prose and computes overlay2−ledger, over-reporting orphaned bytes and paging on accounted-for bytes; or follows the AC and computes root−ledger — two different metrics from one plan.","Images/volumes stored outside overlay2 make the whole-root ledger exceed overlay2, distorting the clamp behaviour."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Adopt the AC's whole-root pairing everywhere: docker_unaccounted_bytes = du(/var/lib/docker) − (images + containers + build cache), clamped at 0; keep the overlay2 du reading only as a diagnostic breadcrumb in the log line, not in the arithmetic. Update the Design section's 'overlay2 truth − ledger' phrase to match.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve whether `docker builder prune --keep-storage` is version-stable across the engines targeted (evidence indicates `--keep-storage` is deprecated for `--max-storage`), and either apply the same engine-version rendering used for daemon.json to the CLI invocations in Design section 1 and autodeploy.sh, or justify why the CLI flag needs no version gate.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"`docker builder prune --keep-storage` applies the same cap on demand; a BuildKit-only flag, used for THIS share only.\"","Plan already treats the daemon.json side as version-dependent: \"Engine 25.0 / BuildKit 0.13 added `policy[].reservedSpace|maxUsedSpace|minFreeSpace` and deprecated `defaultKeepStorage`/`keepStorage`\"","Retrieved: moby/moby issue 50120 — 'Flag --keep-storage has been deprecated, keep-storage flag has been changed to max-storage' (docker builder prune CLI)","Retrieved: buildx issue #458 discusses renaming prune --keep-storage; Docker Docs 'docker builder prune' still lists --keep-storage, indicating a version-straddling flag","The plan's own version-probing rationale ('A wrong key is silently IGNORED — the cap would simply not exist') applies symmetrically to the CLI flag it does not version-gate"],"finding":"The plan version-probes the daemon.json builder.gc schema (maxUsedSpace >= 25.0 vs defaultKeepStorage below) but asserts the CLI `docker builder prune --keep-storage` 'applies the same cap on demand' (Design section 1) and reuses that flag in autodeploy.sh without the same version-awareness; retrieved evidence shows `--keep-storage` is deprecated in favor of `--max-storage` on the same recent engine families, so the on-demand cap may emit a deprecation warning or fail to parse on the engines where the plan correctly renders maxUsedSpace.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feb7c58b6acabf822","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design > 'BuildKit share (5 GiB)' and AC 'autodeploy.sh takes its BuildKit --keep-storage from the shared budget'; infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:392","norm_id":"nbfe88625e86dee60","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Host running Engine >= 28 where `docker builder prune --keep-storage` warns/errors while autodeploy.sh's emergency-prune path invokes exactly that flag","The 'applies the same cap on demand' claim in the runbook/remediation being run by an operator on a newer engine"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have docker-storage-cap.sh emit the correct prune flag for the probed engine version (--keep-storage below the cutover, --max-storage at/above) and have autodeploy.sh consume that resolved flag from the shared budget rather than hardcoding --keep-storage.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"insufficient","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify the `docker builder prune` cap flag against the engine-version range the plan claims portability over (observe `docker builder prune --help`), and either version-select the flag (`--keep-storage` below 25.0, `--reserved-space`/`--max-used-space` at/above) the same way daemon.json is probed, or state why the CLI flag is version-invariant where the daemon.json key is not.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'docker builder prune --keep-storage applies the same cap on demand; a BuildKit-only flag, used for THIS share only.'","Plan establishes version-dependence for the equivalent daemon.json key: 'Engine 25.0 / BuildKit 0.13 added policy[].reservedSpace|maxUsedSpace|minFreeSpace and deprecated defaultKeepStorage/keepStorage. A wrong key is silently IGNORED.'","The parallel CLI change deprecated `docker builder prune --keep-storage` in favor of `--reserved-space` in the same BuildKit generation; the plan applies its version-probe only to daemon.json, not to the prune flag.","grep for `reserved-space` and `max-used-space` across the repo returns no matches — no CLI-flag version-probe exists.","Evidence class: Partially-verified — subcommand `docker builder prune` and `--keep-storage` exist on the incident-era engine, but the flag name is unconfirmed across the version range the plan claims portability over ('Portability: host config + local script tests')."],"finding":"The plan version-probes the daemon.json `builder.gc` schema key (maxUsedSpace >=25.0 vs defaultKeepStorage below) but asserts the sibling CLI flag `docker builder prune --keep-storage` as version-invariant, though the same Engine 25.0 / BuildKit 0.13 change deprecated `--keep-storage` in favor of `--reserved-space`. On a newer Docker CLI the flag can warn or (later) fail, silently defeating the on-demand BuildKit cap — the identical 'a wrong key is silently ignored' failure the plan guards against for daemon.json.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a8649f7280c41e9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section 1 (BuildKit share); AC 'autodeploy.sh takes its BuildKit --keep-storage from the shared budget'; infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:392","norm_id":"ne2aea07db1df763b","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A host provisioned on Docker Engine >= 25.x where the CLI has renamed/deprecated `--keep-storage`: the capped prune em